UML to Java Translation: Association
In UML, associations between classes become field references in Java. A one-to-many association uses a
collection (e.g.,
List
), while a one-to-one association uses a single reference.
import java.util.List;
import java.util.ArrayList;
public class Teacher {
private String name;
// One teacher associated with many students (1..*)
private List<Student> students = new ArrayList<>();
public void addStudent(Student s) { students.add(s); }
public List<Student> getStudents() { return students; }
}
public class Student {
private String name;
// One student associated with many teachers (1..*)
private List<Teacher> teachers = new ArrayList<>();
public void addTeacher(Teacher t) { teachers.add(t); }
}
