UML to Java Translation: Class Diagram
A UML class with its three compartments (name, attributes, methods) maps directly to a Java class. Visibility
markers translate to access modifiers:
+
is
public
,
-
is
private
,
#
is
protected
.
public class Student {
// Attributes (middle section)
private String name;
// - name: String
private int studentId;
// - studentId: int
protected double gpa;
// # gpa: double
// Methods (lower section)
public String getName() {
// + getName(): String
return name;
}
public void enroll(String course) { // + enroll(course: String): void
System.out.println(name + " enrolled in " + course);
}
private boolean validateId() {
// - validateId(): boolean
return studentId > 0;
}
